WEBVTT

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Good day, ladies and gentlemen.
My name is Sugata Eishiro.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
I am currently seeking an assistant.

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:38.292
During the Age of Exploration,

00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:40.958
the man who pioneered a
southern route around the world

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.833
was Ferdinand Magellan.

00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:46.417
His greatest feat was to prove
outright that the world was round,

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:49.875
by use of his colleagues'
navigational logbooks.

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:53.875
The mapmakers of the time
must have been thrown into disarray.

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:57.542
After all, their conception of
the world had been disproved.

00:00:57.542 --> 00:01:00.917
It's possible for the same
thing to happen in our age,

00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:03.583
if only a New World were discovered.

00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:07.542
Incidentally, there is a
reference in the navigational logs

00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:10.625
to some giant footprints,
discovered near Patagonia.

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:13.667
Even now, the possibility of one
surviving on an island somewhere

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.667
is greater than zero.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.083
Would you...

00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:20.917
be my assistant?

00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:25.125
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:27.708
<i>dou shita tte iu no</i>

00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:31.458
<i>mune no beru ga naru</i>

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:37.000
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:42.958
<i>hajimari wa ano toki datta (ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:42.958 --> 00:01:48.583
<i>kimi ga me no mae ni totsuzen (ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:53.792
<i>arawareta no wa umareru mae kara</i>

00:01:53.792 --> 00:01:56.708
<i>kimerarete'ta n da ne</i>

00:01:56.708 --> 00:01:59.583
<i>kitto sou da yo</i>

00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:05.208
<i>negai ya yabou ya kuusou ga</i>

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:10.917
<i>shiranai reberu e doa o tataite</i>

00:02:10.917 --> 00:02:17.125
<i>habataku kagi to mirai o kureru</i>
<i>(with your wings)</i>

00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:20.042
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:02:20.042 --> 00:02:23.042
<i>tomerarenai yo</i>

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:28.625
<i>tenshi ga narashiteru</i>
<i>"daisuki" no aizu da yo ne</i>

00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:31.500
<i>can you hear my heart bell?</i>

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.958
<i>dou shita tte iu no</i>

00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:39.375
<i>kiita koto ga nai mune no beru ga naru</i>

00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:48.500
<i>sore de mo mada kimi</i>
<i>wa nani mo shiranai keredo</i>

00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:59.042
Summer vacation is almost here. It's so hot.

00:02:59.042 --> 00:03:01.333
I'll have to buy a cooler.

00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:03.375
Master, before you do that,

00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:07.083
should you not do something
about where you are living?

00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:09.250
Yeah, you're right. Thanks to those panties,

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.250
the whole house has
been blown to smithereens.

00:03:14.958 --> 00:03:16.292
I know!

00:03:16.292 --> 00:03:19.542
What if we went and
had Sugata put us up again?

00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:23.542
"Hot Night With the Big Fish"

00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:27.083
Sugata!

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:30.042
I hate to drop in out of the blue,

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.667
but could we stay with
you for a little while?

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.583
It's okay with me...

00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:37.083
You mean it? Hooray!

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.375
...but I can't vouch for your safety.

00:03:40.208 --> 00:03:42.042
Look out, Tomoki!

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:50.917
The bears come around here
a lot this time of year. Be careful.

00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:57.458
<i>No good! If we stay here,</i>
<i>we're gonna die!</i>

00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:58.958
Nope.

00:03:58.958 --> 00:04:01.083
Tomo, you're sure to rummage
through my underwear and stuff.

00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:02.875
There's no way you're staying here!

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.708
You're sure you won't come over?

00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:06.375
I can't take the bears!

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:08.458
You can get eaten by them, for all I care.

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:11.000
That's cold, Sohara!
We've been friends since we were kids!

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.500
At a time like this, you've got to help me!

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.833
Well then, can you promise
that if you come into my room,

00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:17.083
you'll stay out of my underwear?

00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.792
Y-Yes, I can do that.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.250
I doubt it.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.708
This looks like fun.

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:25.792
What are you doing?

00:04:26.792 --> 00:04:31.375
Oh, well in that case,
Sakurai, would you like to come over?

00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:34.875
I will do my utmost to be your host.

00:04:34.875 --> 00:04:39.208
Chairman, your house is
the biggest one in town, right?

00:04:39.208 --> 00:04:41.583
That's right! They're huge celebrities!

00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:45.917
If you like, Mitsuki and Sugata,
you can come as well.

00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:48.625
The ultra-celebrity lifestyle...

00:04:57.917 --> 00:04:59.042
We'll come!

00:04:59.042 --> 00:05:03.792
Okay then, that settles it.
Let's head there right now.

00:05:03.792 --> 00:05:05.333
Well, if you'll excuse me...

00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:07.708
Why are you hanging back?

00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:09.875
It isn't like you, Sugata!

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.208
Celebrity! Celebrity!

00:05:16.292 --> 00:05:20.583
I am Mikako's father.
Please, make yourselves at home.

00:05:24.458 --> 00:05:28.708
The Satsukitane Family here
is the clan that has controlled Sorami

00:05:28.708 --> 00:05:31.167
ever since the Edo post town period.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:31.875
"Organized Crime"

00:05:31.875 --> 00:05:35.208
You mean, they're <i>that </i>kind of celebrity?

00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:37.750
Well, you might say that.

00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:42.208
You all don't have to be afraid.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:46.917
It's all right, as long as you don't
do anything <i>too </i>out-of-bounds.

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:54.667
Boss!

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:57.583
S-S-Sorry about that!

00:05:57.583 --> 00:06:01.292
She's not all that bright!
Please, spare our lives!

00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:08.583
We're good.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:14.625
Come on, now, what are you doing?
Hurry up and see to our guests!

00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:16.625
Very good, Sir!

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.125
This is awesome!

00:06:24.125 --> 00:06:25.875
Here you go, young master.

00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:27.792
And this, as well, young master.

00:06:27.792 --> 00:06:30.667
They're addressing Sugata as
"young master."

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:33.542
That's probably because
the chairman and Sugata

00:06:33.542 --> 00:06:36.375
have been close to
each other since they were kids.

00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:41.875
Care to join me elsewhere?

00:06:41.875 --> 00:06:43.708
You mean it?!

00:06:51.708 --> 00:06:56.542
That's it. I can't eat any more.

00:06:57.958 --> 00:06:59.083
Where is Master?

00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:02.375
Oh, Tomo went off to have a bath.

00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:04.083
What? Did you say a bath?!

00:07:04.083 --> 00:07:05.458
Is something the matter?

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.292
Oh, it's just that the
Satsukitane Family has a bath,

00:07:08.292 --> 00:07:09.875
called the "Hell's Gate Bath,"

00:07:09.875 --> 00:07:13.250
that only members of
the clan are allowed to enter.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.542
As long as Tomoki doesn't go
in there by mistake, he'll be fine.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.917
Oh...?

00:07:25.042 --> 00:07:29.542
What's this?
Did you want to come in with me?

00:07:29.542 --> 00:07:32.167
I don't mind if you do.

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:34.125
N-No, I, uh...

00:07:34.125 --> 00:07:36.417
For you to come right on in without asking,

00:07:36.417 --> 00:07:38.917
you're surprisingly aggressive, Sakurai.

00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:40.333
N-No!

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.208
But unfortunately,

00:07:48.417 --> 00:07:50.583
in all seriousness,

00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:55.625
you'd best get out of here right away.

00:07:55.625 --> 00:07:57.750
You could get killed.

00:08:00.375 --> 00:08:03.083
Target at 3 o'clock and fleeing!

00:08:03.083 --> 00:08:08.333
A wanton intruder has entered
the sacred clan's Hell's Gate Bath!

00:08:10.833 --> 00:08:12.458
There he is!

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.042
Hold it, you!

00:08:15.042 --> 00:08:17.958
Give it up!

00:08:17.958 --> 00:08:19.958
I'm gonna get killed!

00:08:23.708 --> 00:08:26.083
Mister, help me!

00:08:27.333 --> 00:08:31.458
I'm sorry. You may be Mikako's friend,

00:08:31.458 --> 00:08:34.458
but our law is absolute.

00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:36.083
Kill him.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.750
Tomo!

00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:40.833
Why?

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.667
The Hell's Gate Bath was once
the place where the celestial maidens,

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:46.667
the ancestors of the Satsukitane Family,

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:49.750
came to purify their heavenly raiment.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.667
However, after the maidens passed away,

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:54.958
and the bath was opened to visitors,

00:08:54.958 --> 00:08:58.000
a divine punishment befell the land of Sorami.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.375
Earthquakes, famine, tempests...

00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:04.625
It is said that they finally subsided

00:09:04.625 --> 00:09:07.792
once the visitors were beheaded.

00:09:07.792 --> 00:09:09.667
Ever since,

00:09:09.667 --> 00:09:12.750
we members of the clan
have enshrined this bath

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:17.833
as the Hell's Gate Bath,
in order to protect the land of Sorami.

00:09:17.833 --> 00:09:23.333
He is Mikako's friend.
See that he suffers as little as possible.

00:09:23.333 --> 00:09:24.292
Yes, Sir.

00:09:24.292 --> 00:09:25.750
Tomo!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.542
Mikako, make them stop!

00:09:27.542 --> 00:09:31.292
I can't. In the Satsukitane Family,
the law is absolute.

00:09:31.292 --> 00:09:37.125
I cannot stop this.
But Ei, you may be able to.

00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:43.250
Stop this!
If you take any further action...

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:48.708
Young Sugata, don't tell me you
would defy the Satsukitane Family.

00:09:58.792 --> 00:09:59.875
You're kidding, right?

00:09:59.875 --> 00:10:01.917
Stop! Please stop!

00:10:01.917 --> 00:10:04.417
You're in my way. Get back!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.417
What are you doing to my master?

00:10:17.667 --> 00:10:21.750
I asked you what you
were doing to my master.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.833
Stop, Ikaros!

00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:10.125
I'm sorry for causing a disturbance.

00:11:10.125 --> 00:11:12.917
It's all right.
Out of respect for the young lady,

00:11:12.917 --> 00:11:15.458
I will allow this to slide tonight.

00:11:15.458 --> 00:11:20.125
She appears to be quite extraordinary.

00:11:20.125 --> 00:11:21.667
Let's go, Ikaros.

00:11:21.667 --> 00:11:24.375
Yes, Master.

00:11:24.375 --> 00:11:26.000
Don't let this bother you.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.417
Yes...

00:11:31.875 --> 00:11:36.625
Mikako, I leave it to you to finish this.

00:11:37.542 --> 00:11:39.167
Yes, Sir.

00:11:42.917 --> 00:11:45.500
Good morning, everyone.

00:11:49.833 --> 00:11:51.417
Good morning.

00:11:51.417 --> 00:11:54.625
Get up, okay? We're almost there.

00:11:54.625 --> 00:11:57.667
Let me welcome you to our desert island.

00:12:03.542 --> 00:12:06.542
What is this?!

00:12:09.917 --> 00:12:14.125
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:12:17.875 --> 00:12:21.417
Wow, the sea is so pretty!

00:12:21.417 --> 00:12:24.458
This island is owned
by the Satsukitane Family,

00:12:24.458 --> 00:12:26.917
so feel free to get as cozy as you like.

00:12:26.917 --> 00:12:30.583
Still, why are we here on a desert island?

00:12:30.583 --> 00:12:33.917
Because someone broke a very important rule,

00:12:33.917 --> 00:12:37.417
making it difficult for
us to stay at the house.

00:12:37.417 --> 00:12:40.583
I'd feel too sorry to
just turn you out, so instead,

00:12:40.583 --> 00:12:43.792
I thought we could spend
some time on our island.

00:12:43.792 --> 00:12:45.333
Have I put you out?

00:12:45.333 --> 00:12:47.458
Oh, no, not at all...

00:12:47.458 --> 00:12:51.292
You would go to this length for Tomo?

00:12:51.292 --> 00:12:54.542
Tomo, you should really thank her!

00:12:54.542 --> 00:12:56.625
Thank you very much.

00:12:56.625 --> 00:12:58.250
My pleasure.

00:13:00.792 --> 00:13:03.583
Since we're here,
I'd like to go take a dip in the ocean!

00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:05.208
Just a moment.

00:13:05.958 --> 00:13:07.958
Don't forget, this is a desert island.

00:13:07.958 --> 00:13:10.917
We should first procure something
to eat, if we're going to get by.

00:13:11.667 --> 00:13:15.708
But this is the chairman's island.
Isn't there a cottage, or something?

00:13:15.708 --> 00:13:18.750
There's nothing here.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.208
That's the shape of it, so you see,

00:13:20.208 --> 00:13:21.792
there's no time for goofing around.

00:13:21.792 --> 00:13:25.958
Let's ask Ikaros and Tomoki
to find something to eat.

00:13:25.958 --> 00:13:28.500
We'll go look for some drinking water.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:30.125
All right.

00:13:31.583 --> 00:13:33.292
Hey, Ikaros...

00:13:33.292 --> 00:13:34.833
Yes, Master?

00:13:34.833 --> 00:13:38.083
Go catch us a suitable
sea bream or tuna or something

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:39.917
from out of the sea around here.

00:13:39.917 --> 00:13:41.667
Yes, Master.

00:13:41.667 --> 00:13:44.167
As long as we're here, let's go extravagant!

00:13:44.167 --> 00:13:45.792
Yes, Master.

00:13:53.083 --> 00:13:55.333
I see some coconut crabs!

00:13:55.333 --> 00:14:00.000
Yay, coconut crabs!
I've always wanted to try them.

00:14:02.917 --> 00:14:08.167
I'm sorry...! Please forgive me...!

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:15.375
<i>It's no use, they nearly killed me.</i>

00:14:15.375 --> 00:14:19.375
<i>Forget about animals,</i>
<i>let's go with plants, instead.</i>

00:14:20.958 --> 00:14:22.875
I'm so hungry.

00:14:23.917 --> 00:14:27.708
Th-Those are clearly
questionable-looking mushrooms.

00:14:27.708 --> 00:14:29.542
But still...

00:14:34.417 --> 00:14:36.625
Oh, no, sweetie!

00:14:36.625 --> 00:14:39.458
Grandpa! Grandpa!

00:14:53.917 --> 00:14:56.625
Did I pass out?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.167
What are those?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.875
Help!

00:15:08.875 --> 00:15:10.500
Sohara?!

00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:19.167
Sohara!

00:15:21.792 --> 00:15:24.500
Hang in there. Are you all right?

00:15:26.958 --> 00:15:30.708
Thank goodness. Tomo, you're okay.

00:15:30.708 --> 00:15:34.542
What happened, Sohara?
I thought you were with Sugata.

00:15:34.542 --> 00:15:38.500
I don't know. We got split up as
we were running away.

00:15:42.042 --> 00:15:43.500
What was that?!

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.542
We heard that thing chasing us,
and ran for our lives.

00:15:46.542 --> 00:15:49.250
I'm scared, Tomo!

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.417
Let's just keep ourselves hidden,
and see what happens.

00:15:52.417 --> 00:15:55.208
Take it easy, Sohara.

00:15:55.208 --> 00:16:00.333
It's all right. We'll go find the
others once it's light out, okay?

00:16:00.333 --> 00:16:01.750
Mm-hmm.

00:16:05.458 --> 00:16:11.417
<i>And then, when morning came,</i>
<i>we went looking for Sugata and Ikaros,</i>

00:16:11.417 --> 00:16:15.750
<i>but days went by,</i>
<i>and we couldn't find them anywhere.</i>

00:16:16.625 --> 00:16:20.292
<i>Come nightfall, we would always</i>
<i>hear that howling.</i>

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:26.667
Tomo, you don't think Sugata
and the others were eaten, do you?

00:16:26.667 --> 00:16:31.250
It's all right. They won't be done in so easily.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.125
Yeah, you're right.

00:16:33.125 --> 00:16:34.458
I'm sure that right now,

00:16:34.458 --> 00:16:37.625
the chairman is on the radio, calling for help.

00:16:37.625 --> 00:16:39.250
Mm-hmm.

00:16:47.542 --> 00:16:49.000
Hey!

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:54.458
Wow! Nice catch, Tomo!
I'll cook them for all I'm worth!

00:16:54.458 --> 00:16:57.208
Yeah, you do that, Sohara!

00:16:57.208 --> 00:17:00.208
<i>And so, a month went by.</i>

00:17:00.208 --> 00:17:03.875
<i>We adapted entirely to life on the island,</i>

00:17:03.875 --> 00:17:07.083
<i>and Sohara got her smile back.</i>

00:17:07.083 --> 00:17:12.333
<i>And just as we began thinking</i>
<i>that life here wasn't so bad...</i>

00:17:21.083 --> 00:17:24.042
What's wrong, Sohara?

00:17:24.042 --> 00:17:29.583
Sorry. I was just thinking
about Sugata and the others.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.917
Say, Tomo, what's going to happen to us?

00:17:35.917 --> 00:17:38.917
If no one comes to rescue us...

00:17:41.375 --> 00:17:44.458
If that happens,
we can just enjoy living here.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.333
I'm here. You're not alone.

00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:53.083
I'm not going to let you
feel lonesome, Sohara, okay?

00:17:53.083 --> 00:17:54.583
Tomo...

00:18:06.208 --> 00:18:11.333
Yeah, sure. And if we have kids,
I'm sure it will be even more lively.

00:18:12.333 --> 00:18:14.375
Have... kids...?

00:18:14.375 --> 00:18:18.583
Oh, no, I didn't mean
it like that! I didn't mean...

00:18:25.333 --> 00:18:28.542
S-Sohara...

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:32.750
T-Tomo...

00:18:51.333 --> 00:18:52.750
Let's get out of here, Sohara!

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:54.208
Mm-hmm!

00:18:58.458 --> 00:18:59.875
Sohara!

00:19:04.542 --> 00:19:06.917
Get moving, legs!

00:19:06.917 --> 00:19:10.000
Damn it, move!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.417
Tomo...

00:19:12.417 --> 00:19:14.458
It's all right.

00:19:14.458 --> 00:19:18.042
I'll be... all right...

00:19:27.083 --> 00:19:31.500
Let Sohara go, you monster!

00:19:35.708 --> 00:19:39.417
Let go! Let Sohara go!

00:19:39.417 --> 00:19:41.042
Let go!

00:19:41.042 --> 00:19:43.042
Let go!!

00:19:44.833 --> 00:19:47.792
Let her go!!

00:20:02.125 --> 00:20:05.042
I have returned, Master.

00:20:05.042 --> 00:20:07.792
I had difficulty finding a school of tuna,

00:20:07.792 --> 00:20:10.042
and went all the way
to the southern hemisphere.

00:20:10.042 --> 00:20:14.625
Tomo, this is seaweed,
and oysters, and stuff.

00:20:14.625 --> 00:20:18.875
What? You mean,
that stuff was just stuck to Ikaros?

00:20:18.875 --> 00:20:21.542
Yes. While I was walking under the sea,

00:20:21.542 --> 00:20:24.667
a lot of things became attached to me.

00:20:24.667 --> 00:20:28.792
So then, what was that howling?
Where are Sugata and the chairman?

00:20:28.792 --> 00:20:33.000
Master, would you like me
to check with my life-sign radar?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.625
Oh, yes, do!

00:20:34.625 --> 00:20:36.625
One moment, please.

00:20:58.083 --> 00:21:00.792
Well, that certainly was entertaining.

00:21:00.792 --> 00:21:03.833
That's what you get for
breaking the law of our clan.

00:21:03.833 --> 00:21:06.333
We'll call it even now.

00:21:06.333 --> 00:21:09.792
I'm not going to let
you feel lonesome, Sohara.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.417
Tomo...

00:21:14.417 --> 00:21:16.750
How nice it is to be young.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:20.750
Look, just be glad that you
didn't have your life taken from you.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.083
And once again, I got dragged into everything

00:21:24.083 --> 00:21:26.042
because of something Tomo did?

00:21:26.042 --> 00:21:28.292
Oh, no! Calm down, Sohara!

00:21:28.292 --> 00:21:30.958
This was all your fault, wasn't it, Tomo?!

00:21:30.958 --> 00:21:33.792
Tomo, you idiot!

00:21:35.458 --> 00:21:37.875
Help me!

00:21:41.875 --> 00:21:45.708
My house is back the way it was! But how?!

00:21:45.708 --> 00:21:48.250
Master, over there.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.458
Ikaros, hello!

00:21:50.458 --> 00:21:51.875
Hello!

00:21:53.875 --> 00:22:00.167
A humble gift from the
Satsukitane Family. Please accept it.

00:22:00.167 --> 00:22:04.292
In the Satsukitane Family,
strength is everything.

00:22:04.292 --> 00:22:08.625
My father seems to have
taken quite a liking to Ikaros.

00:22:21.667 --> 00:22:27.083
"Ikaros' Undersea Adventures"

00:22:27.333 --> 00:22:34.875
<i>Kawaguchi Hiroshi goes into a cave</i>

00:22:34.875 --> 00:22:42.375
<i>He goes in after the cameraman and lighting man</i>

00:22:42.375 --> 00:22:49.917
<i>Inside the cave, a skeleton falls over</i>

00:22:49.917 --> 00:22:53.708
<i>A shiny white skeleton, as though polished by</i>

00:22:53.708 --> 00:22:57.750
<i>something, falls over</i>

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:01.542
<i>Then, all of a sudden, from overhead,</i>

00:23:01.542 --> 00:23:05.333
<i>scary snakes attack</i>

00:23:05.333 --> 00:23:08.750
<i>For some mysterious reason,</i>

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:12.917
<i>they drop tail-first</i>

00:23:12.917 --> 00:23:16.458
<i>After avoiding the snakes' onslaught,</i>

00:23:16.458 --> 00:23:20.125
<i>motionless scorpions attack</i>

00:23:20.125 --> 00:23:24.000
<i>After the scorpions come poisonous spiders</i>

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:28.375
<i>Hiroshi brushes them away barehanded</i>

00:23:29.625 --> 00:23:29.667
<i>Go! Go! Kawaguchi Hiroshi</i>

00:23:29.667 --> 00:23:33.375
<i>Go! Go! Kawaguchi Hiroshi</i>

00:23:33.375 --> 00:23:41.208
<i>Go! Go! Kawaguchi Hiroshi</i>

00:23:41.208 --> 00:23:45.750
<i>Go get 'em!!</i>

00:23:50.167 --> 00:23:53.917
Here are some lunchtime announcements.

00:23:53.917 --> 00:23:59.750
I'm not going to let you feel
lonesome, Sohara, okay?

00:24:00.958 --> 00:24:08.086
Tomo...
